WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.880
An applied force sets an object into forward motion across a surface with velocity v.

2
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:23.110
Even smooth surfaces have countless microscopic hills and valleys when viewed under magnification.

3
00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:38.150
Microscopic irregularities interlock, creating an opposing friction force pointing opposite to motion.

4
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:52.670
The opposing friction continuously reduces speed until the object gradually comes to a complete halt.

5
00:00:52.670 --> 00:01:07.330
Lubricants separate ridges with a fluid layer, and wheels turn heavy sliding into smooth rolling.

6
00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:18.870
Friction is a necessary contact force that opposes motion and allows us to grip, walk, and brake safely.
